        {
          "id": 431503857,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I would like to add it to build CI.  See https://www.wireshark.org/lists/wireshark-dev/202010/msg00056.html, there are currently 221 issues which I'm not thrilled about working through by myself.\n\nRunning the script (without --mask, --label or --consecutive) over all of the dissectors takes a couple of minutes, I think.  Using --commits 1 or --open is likely to be very quick.  I'm pretty sure every error it reports will be a real bug at the moment - the other options require more manual checking of the output.  --mask could maybe be turned on, but it needs to be told about new exemptions (usually multiple reserved or spare fields combined into 1) as they are found.\n\nWould ./gitlab-ci.yml be the right place to look? I can see where it could be added to merge-req:ubuntu-clang-other-tests:",
          "author": {
            "id": 6810036,
            "username": "martin.r.mathieson",
